  "title": "The knot's junction crosses wires softly, never sharply",
  "subject": "Whether a trisum junction of twisted pieces can act as a crossover",
  "conclusion": "With nonnegative counts the junction's not-all-equal square lines can never force a relation between the host's two line-neighbours without pinning them, so no junction is a crossover; its points can carry a wire. Yet twisted truncated-octahedron pieces give soft crossings outside the matchgate class, such as (40000, -1112, 3336, -192), so hardness by interpolation remains open.",
